  "description": "OYAWOD crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C102 H128 Co4 Ho4 N4 O38,4(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ho1 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho4 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho3 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Ho2 (Ho) has 8 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.350-3.608 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.16-109.26°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C106H144Co4Ho4N4O42. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Co(II), Ho(III).",
